  "section_notes": "The final standard is strict on reporting and testing limits, but allows a regulator-approved, time-limited corrective-action pathway for models exceeding the 5% thermal-test failure rate. Remote shut-off retrofits are required within 6 years, fire suppression within 36 months, and mandatory recalls trigger at 8 incidents per 100,000 with prompt customer notice. Per-model test results go to customers and regulators but not the general public."
